{{/* Renders "true" on WSL, "" otherwise -- callers write {{ if includeTemplate "is-wsl" . }}.
Two signals, not one: osrelease usually contains "microsoft", but a WSL kernel can be rebuilt
without that substring and still be WSL, so the binfmt_misc WSLInterop mount (present only
under real WSL) is checked too. One definition here instead of each caller re-inlining the
substring-only test, which is what let them drift out of sync with dot_gitconfig.tmpl. */ -}}
{{- if or (contains "microsoft" (lower .chezmoi.kernel.osrelease)) (stat "/proc/sys/fs/binfmt_misc/WSLInterop") -}}
true
{{- end -}}
